title: The Party in 1922
subtitle: The Zentrale sets the task for the new year.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1922 and month = 1
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.leader();
!}

= The Party in 1922

The mark buys a fifth of what it bought a year ago, and Chancellor [+ chancellor +] promises the Allies he will pay what they ask. [? if march_action = 1 : The party is still counting its losses from the March Action. Lenin told the Third Congress what to do next: win the majority of the working class first. ?][? if march_action = 0 : There was no March Action, and the party kept its members through 1921. Moscow has never quite forgiven it. ?][? if march_action = 2 : The party won in Central Germany last March, and the police have not forgotten it. ?]

[? if levi_split = 1 : Paul Levi sits in the Reichstag with his Working Group and says the Zentrale takes its orders from Moscow. ?][? if left_split = 1 : Ruth Fischer and Arkadi Maslow lead their own group in Berlin and call the Zentrale cowards. ?][? if kapp_outcome = 3 : Germany is still governed by the cabinet the unions made in the Kapp days. ?][? if bavaria_soviet = 2 : The red flag still flies over Munich. ?]

The circular to the districts must say what this year is for.

- @united: Win the majority of the workers.
- @rebuild: Put the party's own house in order.
- @prepare: Get ready for the next fight.

@united
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The united front, in the works and the unions. Brandler's people want this.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any deal with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
RG.e22.against('united_front');
Q.e22_year_line = 1;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
Q.spd_relation += 4;
!}

The circular is one page long. Go into the unions, sit on the works councils, and propose joint action to every worker who will listen.

@rebuild
subtitle: Schools, accounts and a paper workers can read. Steadies the party.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_year_line = 2;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
Q.unity += 6;
!}

The party schools reopen. District treasurers are told to send in their accounts on time, and *Die Rote Fahne* is told to write for workers and not for other communists.

@prepare
subtitle: The old fighters keep their rifles. The police will hear of it.
view-if: offensive_gone = 0 or ultraleft_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_year_line = 3;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
Q.red_guards_arms += 4;
Q.repression += 3;
!}

The men of 1920 and 1921 are asked to keep their weapons oiled and their names on a list.
